10380	{"artifactId":"LLD-315d510cb28100e2-s4","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-315d510cb28100e2-s4-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-18T04:27:43.599Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed draft hooks, forced Task issues, and readiness notices address S004's upstream acceptance criteria.","evidence":"DEF §6.4 requires Epic creation at Define draft (ac15), Story creation at design draft (ac16), unconditional Task issues at plan draft (ac17), and an author-facing failure explanation (ac18). The design explicitly covers each. Both actual draft persistence paths are identified in synthesize.ts and workflow-rpc.ts. [files: docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/DEF.md, src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts, src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts]","action":"Retain this scope; extend notice delivery through the client as identified under change-sites.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Legacy approve-time extras, including comments, run only when the push created the issue.","evidence":"autoPushEpicOnHld calls 'postReviewComment(ops, epicRef, hldJsonPath)' outside the 'adopted === undefined' condition. autoPushTasksOnPlan calls 'postReviewComment(ops, storyRef, planJsonPath)' before its loop, including when every Task already has a ref. Applying the design's blanket created-only invariant would suppress existing review comments and violate solo compatibility. [files: src/workflow/tracker-auto.ts]","action":"Specify legacy behavior per extra and per entry point. Preserve Epic review comments on label adoption and plan review comments on repeated pushes.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Legacy Epic lookup failures fall through to creation, and Task creation is gated by pushTasks.","evidence":"The Epic path uses 'const adopted = found.ok ? found.value ?? undefined : undefined'; the Task path returns skipped when '!cfg.pushTasks'. Existing tests explicitly include 'a failing adoption lookup still leads to a create and does not throw'. [files: src/workflow/tracker-auto.ts, src/workflow/__tests__/tracker-auto.test.ts]","action":"Preserve these behaviors in legacy mode.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The strict loader, policy reader, and phase-free PortResult can be reused with the stated public shapes.","evidence":"loadTracker(repo, needed) checks target, capabilities, and whoAmI before returning PortResult<TrackerPort>. policyReader is explicitly '(repo: string): PolicyResult<TeamPolicy | \"none\">'. PortResult's failure branch contains only ok, reason, and kind, supporting a separate internal creation-phase result. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts, src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, src/workflow/team/policy-reader.ts]","action":"Keep creation-phase information internal and preserve the shared result shape.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Carrying readiness through WorkflowStepDone, RunWorkflowResult, and the workflow.run terminal frame is sufficient to tell the author.","evidence":"The streaming client returns the frame data, but runWorkflowStreaming projects it into only 'path', 'runId', 'verdict', and 'counts'. The terminal run command then renders only '✓ ... done' and review information. The proposed notice would be discarded before reaching this author-facing path. RunWorkflowStreamResult also lacks the new fields. [files: src/mcp/daemon-stream.ts, src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/cli/command.ts, src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts]","action":"Add readiness and notice to the streaming client and CLI service contracts, preserve them in runWorkflowStreaming, and display the failure notice in the terminal run handler.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"appendStoryToDefine and review finding application need content-write classification.","evidence":"appendStoryToDefine constructs 'stories: [...define.body.stories, story]' before writing JSON. resolveReviewFinding assigns 'artifact.body = one.body' only for apply; accept, override, and defer update reviewResolutions. The proposed mixed classifications match these bodies. [files: src/workflow/gates.ts, src/workflow/review/resolve.ts]","action":"Retain the per-operation classifications and revision tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Preserving legacy tracker refs alongside units is necessary for existing consumers.","evidence":"syncTracker skips without meta.tracker.epicRef and iterates storyRefs. autoPushTasksOnPlan reads Define storyRefs, falls back to LLD storyRef, and adopts plan taskRefs. patchTrackerMeta currently preserves prior fields with '{ adapter: \"github\", ...prior, ...patch }'. [files: src/workflow/tracker/refs.ts, src/workflow/tracker/sync.ts, src/workflow/tracker-auto.ts]","action":"Keep the full tracker block and existing string-valued ref maps when adding units.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Adding only units to TrackerMeta fully implements the HLD's sc3 tracker shape.","evidence":"HLD §2 explicitly says 'Only the adapter literal \"github\" is widened to the port’s tracker kind'; §4.3 declares 'adapter?: TrackerKind'. Actual TrackerMeta still declares 'readonly adapter?: \"github\"', and this LLD specifies only a units field addition while keeping every existing field unchanged. [files: docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/HLD.md, src/workflow/tracker/refs.ts, src/workflow/tracker/port.ts]","action":"Include the planned adapter widening and define how patchTrackerMeta preserves or receives the actual tracker kind.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"findIssues is an explicit pending sc1 amendment rather than an existing capability or an unacknowledged s4 redesign.","evidence":"TrackerPort currently declares findIssue but no findIssues. The repository's known-limitations section records the accepted s4 uniqueness decision and describes findIssues as 'proposed to s1 as a sharedContract.methodAdd amendment and to be agreed before the s4 build'. HLD assigns sc3 to s4 and sc1 to s1. [files: src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, docs/plans/team-workflow.md, docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/HLD.md]","action":"Keep the build dependency explicit; do not treat the recorded proposal as approval or implementation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A failed create must be reported as potentially committed, without an immediate unconditional retry.","evidence":"ghCreateIssueTyped retries untyped only for a confirmed issue-type rejection. Its catch explicitly executes 'if (!isIssueTypeRejection(err)) throw err'. The adapter converts that error to a failed PortResult, which carries no proof that remote creation did not occur. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts, src/workflow/tracker/port.ts]","action":"Retain the create-phase uncertainty and lookup-before-retry design.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"When the TESTS markdown write fails, the JSON bytes and revision are guaranteed to be exactly restored.","evidence":"persistTestRecordTask attempts restoration inside a nested try/catch. If restoration fails, it logs 'the json could not be put back after the document failed to write' and throws the original error. Thus the new JSON, and its newly minted revision, can remain despite the caller seeing failure. [files: src/workflow/runners/build/test-record.ts, src/workflow/storage.ts]","action":"Describe and surface rollback failure explicitly, including the possibly inconsistent record state. Add a test where both the markdown write and JSON restoration fail; do not promise unconditional restoration.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each upstream S004 acceptance criterion has a proposed test mapping.","evidence":"Compared against DEF §6.4, the design maps ac15 to Define draft/re-draft tests, ac16 to Story creation/adoption tests, ac17 to forced Task creation and retry tests, and ac18 to failure notices and result propagation. The existing tracker-auto suite provides real fake-exec fixtures and legacy failure regression cases. These are proposed tests, not verified passing implementations. [files: docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/DEF.md, src/workflow/__tests__/tracker-auto.test.ts, src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/cli/command.ts]","action":"Retain the mapping and extend ac18 coverage through the CLI display, since a terminal-frame assertion alone misses the confirmed projection gap.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":3,"med":1,"low":8,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-18T04:27:43.599Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6-astra","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
